       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 30 mg once daily is three times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the typical starting dose. It can be titrated up to 10 mg.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg, tell me and include a short note on the clinical rationale. I can add it to the order. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
